<title>DENMARK: Moeller tops Waterhouse Danish share list.</title>
<headline>Moeller tops Waterhouse Danish share list.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish shipping and energy group A.P. Moeller stock showed the biggest share value growth among major listed Danish companies in a Price Waterhouse survey in the financial daily Borsen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The survey, which assessed the Market Added Value (MVA) of leading Danish companies, said that Moeller's D/S 1912 and D/S Svendborg shares grew by a combined 37 billion crowns, a 175 percent rise, from 1995-96.</p>
<p>Other companies providing shareholders with outstanding returns included holding company Sophus Berendsen, biotechnology group Novo Nordisk, telecoms operator Tele Danmark and brewer Carlsberg.</p>
<p>The table below lists the 10 shares which showed the biggest growth in value from 1995 to 1996 and the nine which performed worst. Only companies which issued full year 1996 results were included in the survey.</p>
<p>MVA expresses a company's total market capitalisation, while RVA (Relative Value Added) rates a share's ability to accrue capital gains for investors.</p>
<p>An RVA rating above one point represents a gain on invested capital, minus ratings show losses.</p>
<p>Company	   MVA 1996	MVA 1995	% change   RVA 1996</p>
<p>		    (billion Dkk) (billion Dkk)		Rating</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller    57.445	  20.914	  175	  2.69</p>
<p>S. Berendsen    16.463	   8.995	   83	  3.77</p>
<p>Novo Nordisk    16.316	   6.177	  164	  1.65</p>
<p>Tele Danmark    14.541	  10.081	   44	  1.46</p>
